Deconvolution library
Copyright 2026 Neurodesk contributors

The WebAssembly module wasm/deconvolution_wasm_bg.wasm is built from the Rust
crates exes/deconvolution/core and exes/deconvolution/wasm (MIT, LICENSE) by
scripts/build-wasm.sh. The Gibson-Lanni PSF, the FFT convolution and the
Richardson-Lucy and RL-TV iterations are written for this package from the
publications cited in README.md; no code of psfmodels, scikit-image or
DeconvolutionLab2 is included. Those tools are used only as external
references by validation/.

The module statically links Rust crates under MIT (or MIT OR Apache-2.0, used
under MIT) and, for unicode-ident, the Unicode-3.0 licence. THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md
holds each crate's licence text verbatim, with its copyright lines; it is
generated from exes/deconvolution/Cargo.lock by
scripts/deconvolution-third-party-notices.py.

libm's Bessel functions j0 and j1 are ported from FreeBSD msun (e_j0.c,
